#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105560 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acc86fb6-2ef4-5f8f-b204-6e1fdbbf0530" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "62405619-31ca-5403-aa45-360e6b3fbd59" :question/math-academy-id "e-3289" :question/problem "Find the area of $\\triangle{ABC}$ below. Round your answer to two decimal places.\n\n![](images/dc/dc625408598aa3cbfda44ec877c9a26ab563dee9fcf757192fcf2cf8411f606a.png)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A}=\\dfrac{1}{2}ab\\sin{C},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\angle{C}$ is between the sides of lengths $a$ and $b.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =CB=58 \\\\ b & =CA=40 \\\\ m∠C & ={31}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\sin{31^{\\circ}} = 0.515\\,038\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 58\\cdot 40\\operatorname{sin}⁡{31}^{∘} \\\\  & =1160\\cdot (0.515\\,038) \\\\  & ≈597.44,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105561 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105905 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3173d361-b91d-5699-97d8-6595ef59d0a3" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/id #uuid "b41b2354-c339-5398-ab43-5886b8447c1c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3294" :question/problem "Rounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD?$\n\n![](images/bc/bc9f32a9c0e8b042498a72e808a29274bd505e786d8ec43d0e0bc9888fdf6e44.png)" :question/worked-solution "The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is the sum of the areas of the triangles $\\triangle ABC$ and $\\triangle ADC$ (see the illustration below).\n\n![](images/ac/acd2e923a65d0821cd59ed8b8274ceb5fc38def896467e37c8b1d454f958699e.png)\n\n First, we find the area for $\\triangle ABC,$ and get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABC} & =\\frac{1}{2}(42)(35)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{36}^{∘} \\\\  & =735\\operatorname{sin}⁡{36}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈432.022\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow we find the area for $\\triangle ADC,$ and get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ADC} & =\\frac{1}{2}(20)(18)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{80}^{∘} \\\\  & =180\\operatorname{sin}⁡{80}^{∘} \\\\  & ≈177.265\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nFinally, we add together the areas of our two triangles to determine the area of $ABCD.$ We get\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABCD} & ={A}_{ABC}+{A}_{ADC} \\\\  & =432.022+177.265 \\\\  & ≈609\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, to the nearest integer, the area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ is $609.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105562 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105906 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5dd3dcff-06d2-5d61-9863-0f5b541d8d4b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle Given the Area of a Quadrilateral"}] :question/id #uuid "472216c8-da7d-58fb-9056-e71d5e33460d" :question/math-academy-id "e-3297" :question/problem "The area of $ABCD$ is $300\\, \\text{cm}^2.$  What is the area of $\\triangle ABC$ rounded to the nearest integer?\n\n![](images/c0/c06ffb123bdd24c3f83419767b6d1578223b8093089b79f91aae8f1fc6121305.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the area of $\\triangle ACD.$ We get \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ACD} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot DA\\cdot DC\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡D \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(25)(32)\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =400\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =375.877... \\\\  & ≈376\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.\n\nThe difference of the areas of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ and $\\triangle ACD$ gives the area of $\\triangle ABC.$ Therefore, \n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{ABC} & ={A}_{ACD}-{A}_{ABCD} \\\\  & =376-300 \\\\  & =76\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105579 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105904 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Angle or Side of a Triangle Given the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "c8d31ea4-41c6-5f24-bf7a-a950a30342d7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4253" :question/problem "The area of ​​the triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is $24\\sqrt{2} \\text{ cm}^2.$ Find $AB.$\n\n![](images/e9/e93e732bd04cfda304c2098087548a638d8d869ccf8b1050235e8207825875d3.png)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A}=\\dfrac{1}{2}bc\\sin{A},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\angle{A}$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB, \\\\ b & =AC=12\\text{ cm}, \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\sin{45^{\\circ}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $c=AB,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 24\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\ 24\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot c\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ 24\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}} & =3\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}c \\\\ 24 & =3c \\\\ c & =8\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AB = 8\\,\\textrm{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278383 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105904 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Angle or Side of a Triangle Given the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a92871f-5bd5-581e-ac06-dbd13021c053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275724} {:answer/id #uuid "299f96e2-93fa-5d8f-ab41-fc313dbd3222" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275854} {:answer/id #uuid "4f831c2c-96bc-514e-94a8-9c7ae9a2e9a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276188} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb62d91-e7c1-5a0b-9594-0da656f39663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276601} {:answer/id #uuid "a89eff61-0284-58bc-8453-86df1e739eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a92871f-5bd5-581e-ac06-dbd13021c053" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275724} :answer-field/id #uuid "e821e218-a2a4-5efe-86d2-0f9a4556c28f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "43fd23a0-08b8-58ee-b7e6-43240cfa05d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-161109" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b95571772af958b4f7b7dcdbba630b78e029c838340dc272809a6c7915dc9c90.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $\\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2}{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $AC.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=6\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC, \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $b=AC,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 6\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot 6\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}\\,b}{2} \\\\ \\frac{21\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}}{\\cancel{2}} & =\\frac{3\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}\\,b}{\\cancel{2}} \\\\ 3b & =21 \\\\ b & =7\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AC=7\\,\\text{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105904 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Angle or Side of a Triangle Given the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55cfe684-dc18-5ab1-b164-6d50fade618a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327676} {:answer/id #uuid "8d23ee9d-454e-5907-a98d-d759e11996ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328151} {:answer/id #uuid "b7359851-720e-5ab4-876a-6265d25f515d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328528} {:answer/id #uuid "cf531d87-8a79-5162-b024-e25dc07d7e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328757} {:answer/id #uuid "e7164a97-e526-5ef2-8ced-7e38b414e248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf531d87-8a79-5162-b024-e25dc07d7e53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328757} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbc9b871-5875-5e5c-8a91-d0aec6bf5882" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329619}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55d7cd50-6834-55b6-a52f-4f6d251b49dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-43339" :question/problem "![](images/85/85b13f2236c5f00da34ea71fdbfc967882fa6e66c347f6ef40c0604391a5d68e.png)\n\nThe area of ​​the triangle $△ABC$ is $15{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.$ Find $m∠A.$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB=5\\,\\text{ cm}, \\\\ b & =AC=12\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $m∠A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 15 & =30\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\frac{15}{30} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡A & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ m∠A & ={30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
